Hi all,
I have got another problem with LVM and the SoftRAID-package. I use the=20
multipath option. And after some work it is running without LVM. But now I=20
want to create a logical volume on a md-device say /dev/md0. Whenever I=20
load the FC/SCSI-HBA driver it detects to SCSI-devices which are the same=20
and that's what I want. I also finally succeeded on creating a physical=20
volume on the md-device. But when I then call vgscan it dumps with a=20
segfault. And it always dumps when I have to paths to the same device and=20
two devicefiles to the same physical hdd (say /dev/sda and /dev/sdb).
Is that OK?
And is there a possibility to get this configuration going??
Any help would be appreciated.
I attached the debug-output of vgscan -d, if anybody is interested... :-)
